\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The protocol turns narrow local teachers into a single, broadly capable model. Under heterogeneous data ($\alpha =0.05$, $N=10$), the global model (blue) reaches three to four times the accuracy of the average local teacher and comes within a few points of the centralized reference, on both vision (ViT-B/32, CIFAR-100) and language (RoBERTa, MPNet, AG-News). The frozen backbone never enters the encrypted aggregation, so the protocol and its cost are unchanged across these scales.}}{7}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:scaling}{{2}{7}{The protocol turns narrow local teachers into a single, broadly capable model. Under heterogeneous data ($\alpha =0.05$, $\Nc =10$), the global model (blue) reaches three to four times the accuracy of the average local teacher and comes within a few points of the centralized reference, on both vision (ViT-B/32, CIFAR-100) and language (RoBERTa, MPNet, AG-News). The frozen backbone never enters the encrypted aggregation, so the protocol and its cost are unchanged across these scales}{figure.2}{}}
\newlabel{fig:scaling@cref}{{[figure][2][]2}{[1][6][]7}{}{}{}}
