\newlabel{fig:ksweep}{{4}{8}{The bounded trajectory matters. With a low temperature the global model stays just above the shared basin and declines gently as the trajectory lengthens (clients drift away from the basin); a high temperature erases the gain and worsens with every step (ResNet-18, CIFAR-10, $\alpha =0.05$)}{figure.4}{}}
