\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {III}{\ignorespaces Comparison with representative federated-learning methods. Reported accuracies are taken verbatim from each source paper at \emph  {its own} setup (dataset, model, $N$, heterogeneity), so the column is context, not a like-for-like ranking; the protocol axes (one-shot, privacy, rounds, communication) are the controlled comparison. Our method is the only one that is simultaneously one-shot, fine-tuning-based, and protected by encryption that adds no accuracy cost.}}{9}{table.3}\protected@file@percent }
